`TypeError: can't compare offset-naive and offset-aware datetimes` — the validator didn't convert. So `_utc = field_validator(...)(to_naive_utc)` direct-assignment pattern isn't being picked up by Pydantic v2. Need the decorator form:

```python
@field_validator("planned_time", mode="before")
@classmethod
def _utc(cls, v): return to_naive_utc(v)
```

Actually in Pydantic v2, the direct assignment `_utc = field_validator("x")(func)` — I thought it works because field_validator returns a decorator that wraps... Let me not guess; use the standard decorator syntax.

Wait, but the error says "offset-naive and offset-aware" — meaning planned_time was still aware when compared with naive utcnow in reschedule. So validator didn't run. Fix with decorator syntax in all three models.

